+
+## iPhone hardware-aware selection — October 13, 2026 preview
+
+The iPhone checkout now probes VideoToolbox's VTIsHardwareDecodeSupported for H.264 (avc1), HEVC (hvc1), and AV1 (av01) once per process. Capabilities are local, are not profile/account settings, and are not persisted or synced. The simulator deliberately skips probing its Mac host and reports unknown capabilities.
+
+All quality modes prefer copies whose advertised codec does not require software decoding on the detected device. Software-only codecs remain ranked fallbacks; early selection waits for other providers before settling on them. Both direct autoplay and the source picker's recommended card use the same policy. Manual/First Stream modes and existing source/debrid filters are preserved. Targets remain 720p Low Data and 1080p Balanced on iPhone; iPad keeps its existing 2160p Balanced target. Highest still favors resolution and disc remuxes among compatible copies. Existing size/readiness penalties still apply; no new 30 GB Mac budget is imposed on phones.
+
+Hardware support is codec-level information, not verification of every codec profile, bit depth, HDR mode, audio track, container, URL, or available decoder resource. Ranking depends on provider metadata; unknown metadata stays usable. This does not measure bandwidth or inspect picture quality.
+
+Validation: catalog-regression/run.sh passes 115 checks, including 13 new checks for probe FourCC values, simulator isolation, AV1-capable/newer device behavior, HEVC fallback, compatible Highest mode, size/phone quality targets, software fallback, early-selection wait, and legacy/manual behavior. Native Debug simulator build and physical-device verification status are recorded in outputs/Mira-iPhone-hardware-validation.md. This source update is not present in the existing Release IPA 161 until a new IPA is built and sideloaded. Do not claim it is already installed on the user's physical iPhone.
